---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Disclaimer | Pro UPI QR";
const description = "Regulatory and legal disclaimer for Pro UPI QR. We are an independent tool and have no official affiliation with NPCI.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12 md:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="rounded-[2rem] border border-white/70 bg-white/85 p-6 shadow-md md:p-10">
      <a href="/" class="text-sm font-bold text-leaf hover:underline">&larr; Back to Generator</a>
      
      <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-forest md:text-5xl">Legal Disclaimer</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-forest/50">Last Updated: August 27, 2026</p>

      <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-forest/80">
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-forest">1. No Affiliation with NPCI / BHIM / UPI</h2>
          <p>
            Pro UPI QR is an independent web utility and is <strong>not associated, affiliated, authorized, endorsed by, or in any official capacity connected with</strong> the National Payments Corporation of India (NPCI), BHIM, Unified Payments Interface (UPI) network, or any governmental regulatory bodies. 
          </p>
          <p>
            The official website of NPCI can be accessed at <a href="https://www.npci.org.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-leaf underline font-semibold">npci.org.in</a>. All official terms, policies, and API specifications relating to Unified Payments Interface are governed by NPCI.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-forest">2. Trademark Disclaimer</h2>
          <p>
            All product names, brand logos, and registered trademarks displayed on this site—including but not limited to <strong>Paytm, PhonePe, Google Pay, GPay, BHIM, and NPCI</strong>—are the exclusive property of their respective owners. 
          </p>
          <p>
            The inclusion of brand-styled template options, brand presets, or brand logos is done solely for consumer convenience (e.g., helping merchants indicate which scanner apps their QR code accommodates). Use of these trademarks does not imply any endorsement, sponsorship, or association between the trademark holders and Pro UPI QR.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-forest">3. No Financial Services Offered</h2>
          <p>
            Pro UPI QR <strong>does not hold funds, execute bank transfers, or act as a bank, payment aggregator, or payment gateway</strong>. Static tools package user input into a UPI URI. Hosted checkout pages display a merchant's QR and status, but money still moves through the payer's UPI app and banking providers.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-forest">4. Payment References Are Not Bank Verification</h2>
          <p>
            A UTR or transaction reference entered by a customer does not prove that a merchant received money. Pro UPI QR labels such submissions as pending. Merchants must verify settlement in their bank or gateway records before marking an order paid, providing goods, or issuing a refund.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-forest">5. Dynamic Redirects and External Sites</h2>
          <p>
            Account holders choose their dynamic QR destinations. Pro UPI QR does not endorse those destinations and cannot guarantee their content or availability. We restrict destination formats and may disable abusive campaigns, but scanners should still inspect the destination and payment details before continuing. Report suspected phishing to <a href="mailto:abuse@proupiqr.in" class="text-leaf underline font-semibold">abuse@proupiqr.in</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-forest">6. Informational Tools</h2>
          <p>
            Calculators, legal or tax summaries, limits, error explanations, and articles are general information, not financial, accounting, tax, legal, or regulatory advice. Rules and provider behavior can change. Check current official sources or a qualified professional before relying on material decisions.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-forest">7. Use at Your Own Risk</h2>
          <p>
            We provide this tool for free to help small business owners and content creators. We offer no guarantees that the QR codes generated will operate uninterrupted, scan correctly on every device, or process without failure. Users must verify the generated QR code by performing a test scan before printing or placing it at payment checkout counters. We accept no liability for any errors, transaction failures, or lost revenue.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-forest">8. DMCA and Copyright Infringement Notices</h2>
          <p>
            We respect the intellectual property rights of others. If you believe that any content or trademark displayed on this website infringes upon your copyright or trademark rights, you may submit a takedown request or notice of infringement to us at <a href="mailto:dmca@proupiqr.in" class="text-leaf underline font-semibold">dmca@proupiqr.in</a>. Please include details of the alleged infringement and your authorization to act on behalf of the owner.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
